body:
Hi there

I tend to go for runs without my phone, and when I return, the only historical data I get is the previous four readings. I'd like to be able to track what happened to my glucose levels during the run.

Reviewing the code, I see that Bluekon.java seems to limit m_minutesBack to 15 whenever the value is over 17 (lines 356-362 in the current git master):

```
// ensure to have min 3 mins distance to last reading to avoid doible draws (even if they are distict)
if (m_minutesBack > 17) {
    m_minutesBack = 15;
} else if (m_minutesBack > 12) {
    m_minutesBack = 10;
} else if (m_minutesBack > 7) {
    m_minutesBack = 5;
}
```

Is there a specific reason that it reduces any age to the most recent 15 minutes? Could I simply rebuild it with those lines commented out, or with a loop which sets any m_minutesBack to the closest multiple of 5, along the lines of this:

```
if ((m_minutesBack % 5) > 2) { 
    m_minutesBack -= m_minutesBack / 5;
}
```
?

Thank you for some very useful software!
